  "decoded_text": "<|im_start|>system\nYou are a concise trip-planning assistant. Use tools for live facts.\n\n# Tools\n\nYou may call one or more functions to assist with the user query.\n\nYou are provided with function signatures within <tools></tools> XML tags:\n<tools>\n{\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"get_weather\", \"description\": \"Return a deterministic weather snapshot.\", \"parameters\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"city\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"City to check.\"}, \"day\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Day label such as today or tomorrow.\"}}, \"required\": [\"city\", \"day\"]}}}\n{\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"estimate_travel\", \"description\": \"Estimate deterministic travel time for a route.\", \"parameters\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"origin\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Starting location.\"}, \"destination\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Destination location.\"}, \"depart_window\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Departure window label.\"}}, \"required\": [\"origin\", \"destination\", \"depart_window\"]}}}\n{\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"reserve_room\", \"description\": \"Reserve a meeting room with an explicit time range.\", \"parameters\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"room\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Room name.\"}, \"start_time\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Local start time.\"}, \"end_time\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"description\": \"Local end time.\"}}, \"required\": [\"room\", \"start_time\"]}}}\n{\"type\": \"function\", \"function\": {\"name\": \"lookup_incident\", \"description\": \"Look up an incident status.\", \"parameters\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"incident_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"description\": \"Incident id in INC-#### format.\"}}, \"required\": [\"incident_id\"]}}}\n</tools>\n\nFor each function call, return a json object with function name and arguments within <tool_call></tool_call> XML tags:\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": <function-name>, \"arguments\": <args-json-object>}\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nPick a better city for an outdoor team lunch today: Seattle or Portland. Check both first.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\nI will check Seattle first, then compare it with Portland.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_weather\", \"arguments\": {\"city\": \"Seattle\", \"day\": \"today\"}}\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\n{\"city\":\"Seattle\",\"day\":\"today\",\"condition\":\"rain\",\"high_c\":12,\"wind_kph\":22}\n</tool_response><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\nSeattle looks wet, so I will check Portland before deciding.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_weather\", \"arguments\": {\"city\": \"Portland\", \"day\": \"today\"}}\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n<tool_response>\n{\"city\":\"Portland\",\"day\":\"today\",\"condition\":\"cloudy\",\"high_c\":16,\"wind_kph\":11}\n</tool_response><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\nChoose Portland. It is cloudy rather than rainy, warmer, and less windy; keep Seattle as the indoor fallback.<|im_end|>",
